    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **287 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-registration cap in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`.\n\n**Change** (`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n- Added a `hasReachedDailyRegistrationLimit()` check that counts owners whose `registrationDate` equals today (`LocalDate.now()`). When 20 owners have already been registered today, `addOwner` returns `400 BAD_REQUEST` before persisting.\n- The check runs at the top of `addOwner`, so the daily cap is enforced regardless of other validation. Seed owners have a `null` registration date and don't count; the `@PrePersist` hook on `Owner` stamps newly-created owners with today's date, so only owners actually registered today count toward the limit.\n\n**Tests** (`OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.java`):\n- `createOwnerRejectedWhenDailyLimitReached` \u2014 after 20 owners registered today, the 21st POST returns 400.\n- `createOwnerAllowedBelowDailyLimit` \u2014 with 19 registered today, a new POST still succeeds (201).",
